IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cbca-core`
IMPORT `cb5-nouns`

-- Canada Business Corporations Act (R.S.C. 1985, c. C-44), PART XXI -- GENERAL: THE DIRECTOR'S DOCUMENTS
-- (ss 258 to 267.1). Layer 1: the law, objectively. Nothing here takes anyone's point of view.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. The text this was encoded from is a plain-text rendering of the Department of Justice
-- Canada consolidation current to 2026-09-30 (last amended 2026-03-26); it is not an official version,
-- and nothing here has been verified against the official text. Contains information licensed under
-- the Open Government Licence - Canada.
--
-- HOW THIS MODULE READS THE TEXT.
--   * A power given to the Director ("the Director may ...") is a BOOLEAN rule that says when the power is
--     open; a duty ("the Director shall ...") says when it is due. What the Director decides to do is not
--     encoded: it is the Director's, and the Director's seat is never taken.
--   * "In the prescribed circumstances" and "the form the Director fixes" are not among the sources: each is a
--     plain BOOLEAN input and no circumstance is invented.
--   * Sections 258.1, 260 and 261 give powers of rule-making, appointment and regulation; they decide no
--     question about a person, so they are rows of the coverage table and not rules (see NOTES.md).

§ `Part XXI -- The Director's documents`

§§ `s 258 and s 258.2 -- copies and exemption`

-- src:3210 | 258 Where a notice or document is required to be sent to the Director under this Act, the Director may accept a photostatic or photographic copy thereof.
@ref CBCA s 258 (src:3210)
GIVEN `a notice or document is required to be sent to the Director under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document sent is a photostatic or photographic copy` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may accept a photostatic or photographic copy within s 258` IF
        `a notice or document is required to be sent to the Director under this Act`
    AND `the document sent is a photostatic or photographic copy`

-- The power is open only "in the prescribed circumstances"; the object is a notice or document containing
-- information similar to that in documents required to be made public under another Act of Parliament or of a
-- provincial legislature, as the Director specifies; the Director may set any conditions.
-- src:3219 | 258.2 In the prescribed circumstances, the Director may, on any conditions that the Director considers appropriate, exempt from the application of any provision of this Act requiring notices or documents to be sent to the Director any notices or documents or classes of notices or documents containing information similar to that contained in notices or documents required to be made public pursuant to any other Act of Parliament or to any Act of the legislature of a province as the Director specifies.
@ref CBCA s 258.2 (src:3219)
GIVEN `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notices or documents contain information similar to that in notices or documents required to be made public under another Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature, as the Director specifies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may exempt the notices or documents from being sent to the Director within s 258.2` IF
        `the circumstances are those prescribed`
    AND `the notices or documents contain information similar to that in notices or documents required to be made public under another Act of Parliament or of a provincial legislature, as the Director specifies`

§§ `s 259 -- proof required by the Director`

-- src:3221 | 259 (1) The Director may require that a document or a fact stated in a document or in any information required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director shall be verified in accordance with subsection (2).
@ref CBCA s 259(1) (src:3221)
GIVEN `it is a document, or a fact stated in a document or in information, required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may require verification within s 259(1)` IF
    `it is a document, or a fact stated in a document or in information, required by this Act or the regulations to be sent to the Director`

-- (2): "by affidavit or by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act before any commissioner for
-- oaths or for taking affidavits": either instrument, before a commissioner. The Canada Evidence Act is not
-- among the sources.
-- src:3223 | (2) A document or fact required by this Act or by the Director to be verified may be verified by affidavit or by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act before any commissioner for oaths or for taking affidavits.
@ref CBCA s 259(2) (src:3223)
GIVEN `it is verified by affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is verified by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is made before a commissioner for oaths or for taking affidavits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the document or fact is verified within s 259(2)` IF
        (    `it is verified by affidavit`
         OR  `it is verified by statutory declaration under the Canada Evidence Act`)
    AND `it is made before a commissioner for oaths or for taking affidavits`

§§ `s 261.1 -- payment of fees`

-- src:3249 | 261.1 A fee in respect of the receipt or copying of any document or other information shall be paid to the Director when it is received or copied, and a fee in respect of the examination, filing or issuance of any document or other information or in respect of any action that the Director is required or authorized to take shall be paid to the Director before the document or other information is examined, filed or issued or the action is taken.
@ref CBCA s 261.1 (src:3249)
DECLARE `Step for which a fee is payable (s 261.1)` IS ONE OF
    `receipt or copying of a document or other information (s 261.1)`
    `examination, filing or issuance of a document or other information, or an action the Director is required or authorized to take (s 261.1)`

-- src:3249 | 261.1 A fee in respect of the receipt or copying of any document or other information shall be paid to the Director when it is received or copied, and a fee in respect of the examination, filing or issuance of any document or other information or in respect of any action that the Director is required or authorized to take shall be paid to the Director before the document or other information is examined, filed or issued or the action is taken.
@ref CBCA s 261.1 (src:3249)
DECLARE `When a fee must be paid (s 261.1)` IS ONE OF
    `when the document or other information is received or copied`
    `before the document or other information is examined, filed or issued or the action is taken`

-- src:3249 | 261.1 A fee in respect of the receipt or copying of any document or other information shall be paid to the Director when it is received or copied, and a fee in respect of the examination, filing or issuance of any document or other information or in respect of any action that the Director is required or authorized to take shall be paid to the Director before the document or other information is examined, filed or issued or the action is taken.
@ref CBCA s 261.1 (src:3249)
GIVEN step IS A `Step for which a fee is payable (s 261.1)`
GIVETH A `When a fee must be paid (s 261.1)`
DECIDE `when the fee must be paid to the Director within s 261.1` IS
    CONSIDER step
    WHEN `receipt or copying of a document or other information (s 261.1)` THEN `when the document or other information is received or copied`
    WHEN `examination, filing or issuance of a document or other information, or an action the Director is required or authorized to take (s 261.1)` THEN `before the document or other information is examined, filed or issued or the action is taken`

§§ `s 262 -- sending of articles and statements; certificates`

-- src:3251 | 262 (1) In this section, statement means a statement of intent to dissolve and a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211.
@ref CBCA s 262(1) "statement" (src:3251)
GIVEN `it is a statement of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `statement within s 262(1)` IF
        `it is a statement of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211`
    OR  `it is a statement of revocation of intent to dissolve referred to in section 211`

-- src:3253 | (2) If this Act requires that articles or a statement relating to a corporation be sent to the Director, on receiving the articles or statement in the form that the Director fixes, any other required documents and the required fees, the Director shall
-- src:3254 | (a) record the date of receipt;
-- src:3255 | (b) issue the appropriate certificate;
-- src:3256 | (c) send the certificate, or a copy, image or photographic, electronic or other reproduction of the certificate, to the corporation or its agent or mandatary; and
-- src:3257 | (d) publish a notice of the issuance of the certificate in a publication generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 262(2) (src:3253-3257)
DECLARE `Duty of the Director on receiving articles or a statement (s 262(2))` IS ONE OF
    `to record the date of receipt (s 262(2)(a))`
    `to issue the appropriate certificate (s 262(2)(b))`
    `to send the certificate, or a copy or reproduction of it, to the corporation or its agent or mandatary (s 262(2)(c))`
    `to publish a notice of the issuance of the certificate in a publication generally available to the public (s 262(2)(d))`

-- All four duties have the same four conditions, joined by "and": this Act requires the articles or statement
-- to be sent to the Director; the Director has received them in the form the Director fixes; with any other
-- required documents; and the required fees.
-- src:3253 | (2) If this Act requires that articles or a statement relating to a corporation be sent to the Director, on receiving the articles or statement in the form that the Director fixes, any other required documents and the required fees, the Director shall
-- src:3254 | (a) record the date of receipt;
-- src:3255 | (b) issue the appropriate certificate;
-- src:3256 | (c) send the certificate, or a copy, image or photographic, electronic or other reproduction of the certificate, to the corporation or its agent or mandatary; and
-- src:3257 | (d) publish a notice of the issuance of the certificate in a publication generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 262(2) (src:3253-3257)
GIVEN duty IS A `Duty of the Director on receiving articles or a statement (s 262(2))`
      `this Act requires that the articles or statement relating to a corporation be sent to the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has received them in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has received any other required documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has received the required fees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the duty is due within s 262(2)` IF
        `this Act requires that the articles or statement relating to a corporation be sent to the Director`
    AND `the Director has received them in the form that the Director fixes`
    AND `the Director has received any other required documents`
    AND `the Director has received the required fees`
    AND CONSIDER duty
        WHEN `to record the date of receipt (s 262(2)(a))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to issue the appropriate certificate (s 262(2)(b))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to send the certificate, or a copy or reproduction of it, to the corporation or its agent or mandatary (s 262(2)(c))` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `to publish a notice of the issuance of the certificate in a publication generally available to the public (s 262(2)(d))` THEN TRUE

-- (3): the day of receipt, or "any later day specified by the court or person who signed". (5) adds, for a
-- certificate of discontinuance only, the day the corporation amalgamates under another Act or is continued.
-- src:3259 | (3) A certificate referred to in subsection (2) issued by the Director may be dated as of the day the Director receives the articles, statement or court order pursuant to which the certificate is issued or as of any later day specified by the court or person who signed the articles or statement.
@ref CBCA s 262(3) (src:3259)
GIVEN `the day the certificate is to be dated as of` IS A DATE
      `the day the Director receives the articles, statement or court order` IS A DATE
      `the day was specified by the court or by the person who signed the articles or statement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate may be dated as of the day within s 262(3)` IF
        `the day the certificate is to be dated as of` EQUALS `the day the Director receives the articles, statement or court order`
    OR  (     `the day was specified by the court or by the person who signed the articles or statement`
          AND `the day the certificate is to be dated as of` GREATER THAN `the day the Director receives the articles, statement or court order`)

-- src:3262 | (5) Notwithstanding subsection (3), a certificate of discontinuance may be dated as of the day on which the corporation amalgamates pursuant to another Act or is continued.
@ref CBCA s 262(5) (src:3262)
GIVEN `it is a certificate of discontinuance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the certificate is to be dated as of is the day on which the corporation amalgamates pursuant to another Act or is continued` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a certificate of discontinuance may be dated as of the day within s 262(5)` IF
        `it is a certificate of discontinuance`
    AND `the day the certificate is to be dated as of is the day on which the corporation amalgamates pursuant to another Act or is continued`

§§ `s 262.1 and s 262.2 -- signatures, execution, publication`

-- The reference to regulations "made under paragraph 261(1)(c.1)" is taken as written; that paragraph, in
-- this text, concerns shareholder proposals under subsection 137(1.1) (see NOTES.md).
-- src:3264 | 262.1 (1) A signature required on a certificate issued by the Director under this Act may be printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate or may be in accordance with the regulations made under paragraph 261(1)(c.1).
@ref CBCA s 262.1(1) (src:3264)
GIVEN `the signature is printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signature is in accordance with the regulations made under paragraph 261(1)(c.1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a signature on a certificate issued by the Director is allowed within s 262.1(1)` IF
        `the signature is printed or otherwise mechanically reproduced on the certificate`
    OR  `the signature is in accordance with the regulations made under paragraph 261(1)(c.1)`

-- (3): several documents of like form, each signed by one or more of the individuals, are deemed one
-- document once duly signed by all the individuals required or permitted to sign.
-- src:3267 | (3) Any articles, notice, resolution, requisition, statement or other document required or permitted to be executed or signed by more than one individual for the purposes of this Act may be executed or signed in several documents of like form, each of which is executed or signed by one or more of the individuals. The documents, when duly executed or signed by all individuals required or permitted, as the case may be, to do so, shall be deemed to constitute one document for the purposes of this Act.
@ref CBCA s 262.1(3) (src:3267)
GIVEN `the document is required or permitted by this Act to be executed or signed by more than one individual` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is executed or signed in several documents of like form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each of the documents is executed or signed by one or more of the individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are duly executed or signed by all individuals required or permitted to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the documents are deemed to constitute one document within s 262.1(3)` IF
        `the document is required or permitted by this Act to be executed or signed by more than one individual`
    AND `it is executed or signed in several documents of like form`
    AND `each of the documents is executed or signed by one or more of the individuals`
    AND `the documents are duly executed or signed by all individuals required or permitted to do so`

-- src:3269 | 262.2 The Director must publish, in a publication generally available to the public, a notice of any decision made by the Director granting an application made under subsection 2(6), 10(2), 21.303(3), 82(3) or 151(1), section 156 or subsection 171(2) or 187(11).
@ref CBCA s 262.2 (src:3269)
DECLARE `Application whose grant the Director must publish (s 262.2)` IS ONE OF
    `an application under subsection 2(6) (s 262.2)`
    `an application under subsection 10(2) (s 262.2)`
    `an application under subsection 21.303(3) (s 262.2)`
    `an application under subsection 82(3) (s 262.2)`
    `an application under subsection 151(1) (s 262.2)`
    `an application under section 156 (s 262.2)`
    `an application under subsection 171(2) (s 262.2)`
    `an application under subsection 187(11) (s 262.2)`
    `any other application (s 262.2)`

-- src:3269 | 262.2 The Director must publish, in a publication generally available to the public, a notice of any decision made by the Director granting an application made under subsection 2(6), 10(2), 21.303(3), 82(3) or 151(1), section 156 or subsection 171(2) or 187(11).
@ref CBCA s 262.2 (src:3269)
GIVEN application IS A `Application whose grant the Director must publish (s 262.2)`
      `the Director has made a decision granting the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must publish a notice of the decision within s 262.2` IF
        `the Director has made a decision granting the application`
    AND CONSIDER application
        WHEN `an application under subsection 2(6) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under subsection 10(2) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under subsection 21.303(3) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under subsection 82(3) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under subsection 151(1) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under section 156 (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under subsection 171(2) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an application under subsection 187(11) (s 262.2)` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `any other application (s 262.2)` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 263 and s 263.1 -- annual return and certificates`

-- "Every corporation shall send": the duty is met only by a return in the form and within the period the
-- Director fixes; the three must all hold.
-- src:3271 | 263 Every corporation shall send to the Director an annual return in the form and within the period that the Director fixes.
@ref CBCA s 263 (src:3271)
GIVEN `the corporation has sent the Director an annual return` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the form that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was sent within the period that the Director fixes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the corporation has complied with the duty to send an annual return within s 263` IF
        `the corporation has sent the Director an annual return`
    AND `it is in the form that the Director fixes`
    AND `it was sent within the period that the Director fixes`

-- src:3273 | 263.1 (1) The Director may provide any person with a certificate stating that a corporation
-- src:3274 | (a) has sent to the Director a document or other information required to be sent under this Act;
-- src:3275 | (b) has paid all required fees; or
-- src:3276 | (c) exists as of a certain date.
@ref CBCA s 263.1(1) (src:3273-3276)
DECLARE `Statement the Director may certify about a corporation (s 263.1(1))` IS ONE OF
    `that it has sent to the Director a document or other information required to be sent under this Act (s 263.1(1)(a))`
    `that it has paid all required fees (s 263.1(1)(b))`
    `that it exists as of a certain date (s 263.1(1)(c))`
    `any other statement (s 263.1(1))`

-- src:3273 | 263.1 (1) The Director may provide any person with a certificate stating that a corporation
-- src:3274 | (a) has sent to the Director a document or other information required to be sent under this Act;
-- src:3275 | (b) has paid all required fees; or
-- src:3276 | (c) exists as of a certain date.
@ref CBCA s 263.1(1) (src:3273-3276)
GIVEN statement IS A `Statement the Director may certify about a corporation (s 263.1(1))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may provide any person with a certificate of the statement within s 263.1(1)` IF
    CONSIDER statement
    WHEN `that it has sent to the Director a document or other information required to be sent under this Act (s 263.1(1)(a))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `that it has paid all required fees (s 263.1(1)(b))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `that it exists as of a certain date (s 263.1(1)(c))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `any other statement (s 263.1(1))` THEN FALSE

-- (2): "for greater certainty": the Director may refuse a certificate of existence on knowledge of either
-- kind of default.
-- src:3278 | (2) For greater certainty, the Director may refuse to issue a certificate described in paragraph (1)(c) if the Director has knowledge that the corporation is in default of sending a document or other information required to be sent under this Act or is in default of paying a required fee.
@ref CBCA s 263.1(2) (src:3278)
GIVEN statement IS A `Statement the Director may certify about a corporation (s 263.1(1))`
      `the Director has knowledge that the corporation is in default of sending a document or other information required to be sent under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has knowledge that the corporation is in default of paying a required fee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may refuse to issue a certificate of existence within s 263.1(2)` IF
        statement EQUALS `that it exists as of a certain date (s 263.1(1)(c))`
    AND (    `the Director has knowledge that the corporation is in default of sending a document or other information required to be sent under this Act`
         OR  `the Director has knowledge that the corporation is in default of paying a required fee`)

§§ `s 264 and s 265 -- alteration and corrections`

-- src:3280 | 264 The Director may alter a notice or document, other than an affidavit or statutory declaration, if authorized by the person who sent the document or by that person’s representative.
@ref CBCA s 264 (src:3280)
GIVEN `the document is an affidavit or a statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the alteration is authorized by the person who sent the document or by that person's representative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may alter a notice or document within s 264` IF
        (NOT `the document is an affidavit or a statutory declaration`)
    AND `the alteration is authorized by the person who sent the document or by that person's representative`

-- Hohfeld: the duty is the directors' or shareholders' of the corporation; the Director holds the claim.
-- src:3282 | 265 (1) If there is an error in articles, a notice, a certificate or other document, the directors or shareholders of the corporation shall, on the request of the Director, pass the resolutions and send to the Director the documents required to comply with this Act, and take such other steps as the Director may reasonably require so that the Director may correct the document.
@ref CBCA s 265(1) (src:3282)
GIVEN `there is an error in articles, a notice, a certificate or other document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director has requested the correction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the directors or shareholders must pass the resolutions and take the steps within s 265(1)` IF
        `there is an error in articles, a notice, a certificate or other document`
    AND `the Director has requested the correction`

-- src:3284 | (2) Before proceeding under subsection (1), the Director must be satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 265(2) (src:3284)
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may proceed under subsection 265(1) within s 265(2)` IF
    `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation`

-- (3): (a) the directors approve, unless the error is obvious or the Director's own; (b) the Director is
-- satisfied on both counts. The requester is "the corporation or any other interested person".
-- src:3286 | (3) The Director may, at the request of the corporation or of any other interested person, accept a correction to any of the documents referred to in subsection (1) if
-- src:3287 | (a) the correction is approved by the directors of the corporation, unless the error is obvious or was made by the Director; and
-- src:3288 | (b) the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation and that the correction reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators, as the case may be.
@ref CBCA s 265(3) (src:3286-3288)
GIVEN `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the correction is approved by the directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error is obvious` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the error was made by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the correction reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may accept the correction within s 265(3)` IF
        `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person`
    AND (    `the correction is approved by the directors of the corporation`
         OR  `the error is obvious`
         OR  `the error was made by the Director`)
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the correction would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation`
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the correction reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators`

-- (4): the view of any one of the Director, the corporation or the interested person that the correction
-- would prejudice shareholders or creditors lets that one apply to the court.
-- src:3290 | (4) If, in the view of the Director, of the corporation or of any interested person who wishes a correction, a correction to any of the documents referred to in subsection (1) would prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of a corporation, the Director, the corporation or the person, as the case may be, may apply to the court for an order that the document be corrected and for an order determining the rights of the shareholders or creditors.
@ref CBCA s 265(4) (src:3290)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
      `in the view of the applicant a correction to any of the documents would prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an interested person who wishes a correction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may apply to the court for an order that the document be corrected within s 265(4)` IF
        `in the view of the applicant a correction to any of the documents would prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation`
    AND (    applicant EQUALS `the Director`
         OR  applicant EQUALS `the corporation`
         OR  `the applicant is an interested person who wishes a correction`)

-- src:3292 | (5) An applicant under subsection (4) shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is entitled to appear and to be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 265(5) (src:3292)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant under subsection 265(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 265(5)` IF
    `the person is an applicant under subsection 265(4)`

-- src:3294 | (6) The Director may demand the surrender of the original document, and may issue a corrected certificate or file the corrected articles, notice or other document.
@ref CBCA s 265(6) (src:3294)
GIVEN `a correction is being made under section 265` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may demand the surrender of the original document within s 265(6)` IF
    `a correction is being made under section 265`

-- (7): the corrected document bears the date of the document it replaces, unless the correction is of the
-- date (then the corrected date) or the court decides otherwise. If both exceptions apply the court's
-- decision is taken to prevail (fork F-265(7)-1 in NOTES.md).
-- src:3296 | (7) A corrected document shall bear the date of the document it replaces unless
-- src:3297 | (a) the correction is made with respect to the date of the document, in which case the document shall bear the corrected date; or
-- src:3298 | (b) the court decides otherwise.
@ref CBCA s 265(7) (src:3296-3298)
GIVEN `the date of the document it replaces` IS A DATE
      `the correction is made with respect to the date of the document` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the corrected date` IS A DATE
      `the date the court decides the corrected document is to bear` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `the date the corrected document bears within s 265(7)` IS
    CONSIDER `the date the court decides the corrected document is to bear`
    WHEN JUST d THEN d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN IF `the correction is made with respect to the date of the document`
                      THEN `the corrected date`
                      ELSE `the date of the document it replaces`

-- src:3300 | (8) If a corrected certificate materially amends the terms of the original certificate, the Director shall without delay give notice of the correction in a publication generally available to the public.
@ref CBCA s 265(8) (src:3300)
GIVEN `a corrected certificate materially amends the terms of the original certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must without delay give notice of the correction within s 265(8)` IF
    `a corrected certificate materially amends the terms of the original certificate`

§§ `s 265.1 -- cancellation of articles`

-- src:3302 | 265.1 (1) In the prescribed circumstances, the Director may cancel the articles and related certificate of a corporation.
@ref CBCA s 265.1(1) (src:3302)
GIVEN `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may cancel the articles and related certificate within s 265.1(1)` IF
    `the circumstances are those prescribed`

-- src:3304 | (2) Before proceeding under subsection (1), the Director must be satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation.
@ref CBCA s 265.1(2) (src:3304)
GIVEN `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may proceed under subsection 265.1(1) within s 265.1(2)` IF
    `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation`

-- src:3306 | (3) In the prescribed circumstances, the Director may, at the request of a corporation or of any other interested person, cancel the articles and related certificate of the corporation if
-- src:3307 | (a) the cancellation is approved by the directors of the corporation; and
-- src:3308 | (b) the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation and that the cancellation reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators, as the case may be.
@ref CBCA s 265.1(3) (src:3306-3308)
GIVEN `the circumstances are those prescribed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the cancellation is approved by the directors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may cancel at the request of the corporation or an interested person within s 265.1(3)` IF
        `the circumstances are those prescribed`
    AND `the request is made by the corporation or any other interested person`
    AND `the cancellation is approved by the directors of the corporation`
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation would not prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation`
    AND `the Director is satisfied that the cancellation reflects the original intention of the corporation or the incorporators`

-- src:3310 | (4) If, in the view of the Director, of the corporation or of any interested person who wishes a cancellation, a cancellation of articles and a related certificate would prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of a corporation, the Director, the corporation or the person, as the case may be, may apply to the court for an order that the articles and certificate be cancelled and for an order determining the rights of the shareholders or creditors.
@ref CBCA s 265.1(4) (src:3310)
GIVEN applicant IS A Party
      `in the view of the applicant a cancellation of articles and a related certificate would prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is an interested person who wishes a cancellation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant may apply to the court for an order that the articles and certificate be cancelled within s 265.1(4)` IF
        `in the view of the applicant a cancellation of articles and a related certificate would prejudice any of the shareholders or creditors of the corporation`
    AND (    applicant EQUALS `the Director`
         OR  applicant EQUALS `the corporation`
         OR  `the applicant is an interested person who wishes a cancellation`)

-- src:3312 | (5) An applicant under subsection (4) shall give the Director notice of the application, and the Director is entitled to appear and to be heard in person or by counsel.
@ref CBCA s 265.1(5) (src:3312)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant under subsection 265.1(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant must give the Director notice within s 265.1(5)` IF
    `the person is an applicant under subsection 265.1(4)`

-- src:3314 | (6) The Director may demand the surrender of a cancelled certificate.
@ref CBCA s 265.1(6) (src:3314)
GIVEN `a certificate has been cancelled under section 265.1` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may demand the surrender of the cancelled certificate within s 265.1(6)` IF
    `a certificate has been cancelled under section 265.1`

§§ `s 266 and s 266.1 -- examination of documents; information not to be made available`

-- The person has paid the required fee; the time is usual business hours; the document is one "required to
-- be sent to the Director under this Act" or to a person performing a similar function under prior
-- legislation; and it is none of the three excepted things.
-- src:3316 | 266 (1) A person who has paid the required fee is entitled during usual business hours to examine and make copies of or take extracts from a document or other information — except any information sent under section 21.21, an application referred to in subsection 21.303(3) and any related document and a report sent to the Director under subsection 230(2) — that is required to be sent to the Director under this Act or that was required to be sent to a person performing a similar function under prior legislation.
@ref CBCA s 266(1) (src:3316)
GIVEN `the person has paid the required fee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is during usual business hours` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or other information is required to be sent to the Director under this Act, or was required to be sent to a person performing a similar function under prior legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is information sent under section 21.21` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 21.21 (piece cb1)
      `it is an application referred to in subsection 21.303(3) or a related document` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 21.303 (piece cb1)
      `it is a report sent to the Director under subsection 230(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a person is entitled to examine and make copies or extracts within s 266(1)` IF
        `the person has paid the required fee`
    AND `it is during usual business hours`
    AND `the document or other information is required to be sent to the Director under this Act, or was required to be sent to a person performing a similar function under prior legislation`
    AND (NOT `it is information sent under section 21.21`)
    AND (NOT `it is an application referred to in subsection 21.303(3) or a related document`)
    AND (NOT `it is a report sent to the Director under subsection 230(2)`)

-- src:3318 | (2) The Director shall, on request, provide any person with a copy, extract, certified copy or certified extract of a document that may be examined under subsection (1).
@ref CBCA s 266(2) (src:3318)
GIVEN `a person has requested a copy, extract, certified copy or certified extract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document may be examined under subsection 266(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must provide the copy or extract within s 266(2)` IF
        `a person has requested a copy, extract, certified copy or certified extract`
    AND `the document may be examined under subsection 266(1)`

-- (3) of s 266.1: "wrongdoing includes" the three listed things. "Includes" is not "means", so the ordinary
-- meaning of the word is an input beside the list.
-- src:3324 | (3) In this section, wrongdoing includes
-- src:3325 | (a) a contravention of any provision of this Act or the regulations;
-- src:3326 | (b) the formation of a corporation for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose; or
-- src:3327 | (c) any fraudulent or dishonest actions of persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of a corporation.
@ref CBCA s 266.1(3) (src:3324-3327)
GIVEN `it is a wrongdoing in the ordinary meaning of the word` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a contravention of any provision of this Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is the formation of a corporation for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a fraudulent or dishonest action of persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `wrongdoing within s 266.1(3)` IF
        `it is a wrongdoing in the ordinary meaning of the word`
    OR  `it is a contravention of any provision of this Act or the regulations`
    OR  `it is the formation of a corporation for a fraudulent or unlawful purpose`
    OR  `it is a fraudulent or dishonest action of persons concerned with the formation, business or affairs of a corporation`

-- (1): the information that could reasonably be expected to reveal the identity of a person who, on their own
-- initiative, provides information on the commission or potential commission of a wrongdoing, or any
-- information they provided, unless they consent.
-- src:3320 | 266.1 (1) The Director shall not make available any information that could reasonably be expected to reveal the identity of a person who, on their own initiative, provides information relating to the commission or potential commission of a wrongdoing, or any information provided by the person in relation to the commission or potential commission, unless the person providing the information consents to its being made available.
@ref CBCA s 266.1(1) (src:3320)
GIVEN `the person provided the information on their own initiative` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information relates to the commission or potential commission of a wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the information could reasonably be expected to reveal the identity of the person, or is information the person provided in relation to the wrongdoing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person providing the information consents to its being made available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must not make the information available within s 266.1(1)` IF
        `the person provided the information on their own initiative`
    AND `the information relates to the commission or potential commission of a wrongdoing`
    AND `the information could reasonably be expected to reveal the identity of the person, or is information the person provided in relation to the wrongdoing`
    AND (NOT `the person providing the information consents to its being made available`)

-- src:3322 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the Director may provide information referred to in that subsection to an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2), the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada or any prescribed entity.
@ref CBCA s 266.1(2) (src:3322)
DECLARE `Recipient of protected information (s 266.1(2))` IS ONE OF
    `an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2) (s 266.1(2))`
    `the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada (s 266.1(2))`
    `a prescribed entity (s 266.1(2))`
    `anyone else (s 266.1(2))`

-- src:3322 | (2) Despite subsection (1), the Director may provide information referred to in that subsection to an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2), the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada or any prescribed entity.
@ref CBCA s 266.1(2) (src:3322)
GIVEN recipient IS A `Recipient of protected information (s 266.1(2))`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director may provide the information to the recipient within s 266.1(2)` IF
    CONSIDER recipient
    WHEN `an investigative body referred to in subsection 21.31(2) (s 266.1(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Financial Transactions and Reports Analysis Centre of Canada (s 266.1(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a prescribed entity (s 266.1(2))` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `anyone else (s 266.1(2))` THEN FALSE

§§ `s 267 and s 267.1 -- keeping documents; form of publication`

-- src:3329 | 267 (1) Documents that are received and accepted by the Director under this Act or that were received and accepted by a person performing a similar function under prior legislation shall be kept by the Director, in any form.
@ref CBCA s 267(1) (src:3329)
GIVEN `the document was received and accepted by the Director under this Act, or by a person performing a similar function under prior legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must keep the document within s 267(1)` IF
    `the document was received and accepted by the Director under this Act, or by a person performing a similar function under prior legislation`

-- src:3331 | (2) If documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form,
-- src:3332 | (a) the Director shall furnish any copy required to be furnished under subsection 266(2) in intelligible form; and
-- src:3333 | (b) a report reproduced from those documents, if it is certified by the Director, is admissible in evidence to the same extent as the original documents would have been.
@ref CBCA s 267(2) (src:3331-3333)
GIVEN `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director must furnish a copy in intelligible form within s 267(2)(a)` IF
    `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form`

-- src:3333 | (b) a report reproduced from those documents, if it is certified by the Director, is admissible in evidence to the same extent as the original documents would have been.
@ref CBCA s 267(2)(b) (src:3333)
GIVEN `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a report reproduced from those documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is certified by the Director` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the report is admissible in evidence to the same extent as the originals within s 267(2)(b)` IF
        `documents are kept by the Director otherwise than in written form`
    AND `it is a report reproduced from those documents`
    AND `it is certified by the Director`

-- (3): the Director need not keep or produce a document after the prescribed period, except a certificate
-- with its attached articles or statement received under s 262 and other prescribed documents. The period is
-- prescribed (not among the sources), so its last day is an input.
-- src:3335 | (3) The Director is not required to keep or produce any document or class of documents — other than a certificate and any attached articles or statement received under section 262 and other prescribed documents or prescribed class of documents — after the end of the period prescribed for the keeping or production of the document or class of documents.
@ref CBCA s 267(3) (src:3335)
GIVEN `it is a certificate with any attached articles or statement received under section 262, or another prescribed document or class of documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date it is asked whether the Director is required to keep or produce the document` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period prescribed for keeping or producing the document` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director is required to keep or produce the document within s 267(3)` IF
        `it is a certificate with any attached articles or statement received under section 262, or another prescribed document or class of documents`
    OR  `the date it is asked whether the Director is required to keep or produce the document` AT MOST `the last day of the period prescribed for keeping or producing the document`

-- src:3337 | 267.1 Information or notices required by this Act to be summarized in a publication generally available to the public or published by the Director may be made available to the public or published by any system of mechanical or electronic data processing or by any other information storage device that is capable of reproducing any required information or notice in intelligible form within a reasonable time.
@ref CBCA s 267.1 (src:3337)
GIVEN `the system or device is a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or another information storage device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is capable of reproducing any required information or notice in intelligible form within a reasonable time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `information or notices may be made available or published by the system or device within s 267.1` IF
        `the system or device is a system of mechanical or electronic data processing or another information storage device`
    AND `it is capable of reproducing any required information or notice in intelligible form within a reasonable time`
